  "findings": [
    "The neutral reader message covers several different pipeline failures. Held formula count is not a count of visible placeholder messages.",
    "The single-identifier check rejects sans-serif/bold/script variants as well as actual character or structure disagreements; the 22 held identifiers are not all safe to accept.",
    "The complete-source alignment gate relies on linear OCR which can flatten powers or omit fractions, even when image recognition recovers structure.",
    "Unrelated footer and bullet content was routed as formula candidates.",
    "Two 90-degree expressions differ from the OCR token stream only by a trailing period in MathML.",
    "Two candidates fail MathJax parsing of recognizer LaTeX; MathCAT is skipped for those.",
    "Other valid raw MathCAT speech is withheld by consistency/merge gates, so changing ClearSpeak alone does not solve these failures."
  ],
  "proposed_priorities": [
    "Separate ordinary text, heading/list markers and footers from formula proposals.",
    "Handle a verified one-letter scalar/font presentation case without weakening checks for letter identity, case, vector semantics or extra structure.",
    "Recognize complete expressions and associate sentence punctuation outside their mathematical token comparison.",
    "Keep true recognition ambiguity visible and retain raw artifacts; do not hide it with guessed formulas."
  ]
}
